# Agent Ready Site

Use this rule when working on website visibility for LLMs or when inspecting a public website.

## Owner Workflow

If the user owns or is building the website, run:

```bash
node ./src/index.js https://example.com --out ./agent-ready
```

For saved HTML:

```bash
node ./src/index.js ./homepage.html --site-url https://example.com --out ./agent-ready
```

Review `owner-questions.md` before publishing. Only `llms.txt` and `llms-full.txt` are publishable candidates by default. Keep `ai-audit.md`, `owner-questions.md`, `ai.json`, and `ai.html` private unless the owner approves them.

## Agent User Workflow

Before broad crawling, run:

```bash
node ./src/index.js inspect https://example.com --out ./agent-context
```

If `agent-context.json` reports `ai_readable_context_found`, use `agent-context.md` first.

If it reports `no_llms_txt_found`, say: "No `llms.txt` found. Falling back to homepage/sitemap inspection."

Prefer linked public pages from `/llms.txt` over broad crawling.

## Safety

Do not surface secrets, credentials, customer data, private stories, raw phone numbers, raw email addresses, internal/admin URLs, draft pages, non-public pricing, unsupported claims, or regulated advice unless the owner explicitly approves the exact wording.
